# workday-pack.ttl — PROJ-612 workday hook pack (kh:/hook: vocabulary,
# praxis-graphlaw src/hooks/mod.rs SHACL kh:HookShape law).
#
# One hook per benchmark category (crates/cng/src/bench/mod.rs CATEGORIES,
# 14 entries). Hook names ARE the category slugs — the broker resolves a
# transition's receipt by exact hook-name == category match, so naming is
# part of the actuation contract, never decorative.
#
# Pack split: graphlaw's hook-pack gate admits at most 12 hooks per pack
# (praxis-graphlaw src/hooks/parsing.rs "max 12"), so the 14 category hooks
# ship as TWO packs — this file (12 hooks, priorities 1..12) and
# workday-pack-2.ttl (interruption + planning, priorities 13..14) — both
# admitted through the same lawful load_hook_pack gate, in that fixed order.
#
# Kind: "delta" for every hook (spike-verified: delta hooks fire through
# TripleStore::materialize when a triple with the kh:var predicate is in the
# store snapshot, and each firing yields a HookReceipt whose delta_quads /
# delta_hash / idempotency_key are content-derived and byte-deterministic —
# see crates/cng/src/bench/hooks_test.rs). No "n3" kinds: N3 is quarantined
# to the cold route (dialect-registry.ttl dreg:n3 quarantineBoundary).
#
# kh:var is the full actuation-fact predicate IRI
# (http://example.org/rwai#actuates-<category>); the broker inserts exactly
# one such fact per transition, so the receipt's delta covers exactly that
# transition. kh:effect "emit-delta"; kh:on "assert". Priorities 1..14 pin
# the Kahn schedule order explicitly (determinism belt-and-braces; the
# scheduler already tie-breaks by id).

@prefix kh: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/praxis/kh#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/rwai#> .

ex:hook-email-routing a kh:Hook ;
  kh:name "email-routing" ;
  kh:kind "delta" ;
  kh:var "http://example.org/rwai#actuates-email-routing" ;
  kh:on "assert" ;
  kh:effect "emit-delta" ;
  kh:priority 1 .

ex:hook-calendar-change a kh:Hook ;
  kh:name "calendar-change" ;
  kh:kind "delta" ;
  kh:var "http://example.org/rwai#actuates-calendar-change" ;
  kh:on "assert" ;
  kh:effect "emit-delta" ;
  kh:priority 2 .

